  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Isoliquiritigenin and TAR DNA-binding protein 43 through a series of target interactions. Isoliquiritigenin is implicated in targeting two distinct enzymes, UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B15 and UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10, both of which are targeted by Marlignan J. Marlignan J, in turn, is linked to the TAR DNA-binding protein 43. This indicates that Isoliquiritigenin may influence the activity of Marlignan J, which then affects the TAR DNA-binding protein 43. Additionally, Isoliquiritigenin is also shown to target another enzyme, Electron transfer flavoprotein-ubiquinone oxidoreductase, which is targeted by Vertilecanin B methy ester, which also targets TAR DNA-binding protein 43. The evidence suggests that Isoliquiritigenin may exert its biological effects through multiple pathways, potentially modulating the activity of enzymes that ultimately influence the TAR DNA-binding protein 43. The strength of the evidence is consistent across different paths, but the exact mechanism by which Isoliquiritigenin influences the TAR DNA-binding protein 43 remains to be fully elucidated.",
